    ​[head=1]CONTRACT[/head]
    
    Between [bold]SCP-049[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as the "Plague Doctor") and [bold]SCP Foundation[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as the Foundation)
    
    ​[head=3]1. CONTRACT PURPOSE[/head]
    This contract establishes the rules for containment, interaction, and the limitations on rights and obligations of the Plague Doctor and Foundation personnel. It is intended to ensure personnel safety, preserve the scientific utility of the object, and prevent abuse of privileges by either party.
    
    ​[head=3]2. PARTIES AND DEFINITIONS[/head]
    ​[bullet][bold]Plague Doctor[/bold] — an object identified as SCP-049.
    ​[bullet][bold]The Foundation[/bold] — the organization responsible for the containment, study, and control of SCP-049.
    ​[bullet][bold]Foundation staff[/bold] — facility employees who hold an access card indicating their clearance level and legitimacy records in the staff registry console.
    ​[bullet][bold]Emergency situation (ESO)[/bold] — an event that presents an immediate threat to life and/or facility integrity and/or staff safety (containment breach, armed confrontation, etc.).
    
    ​[head=3]3. GENERAL PROVISIONS[/head]
    ​[bullet]The Plague Doctor has signed this contract and thereby confirms understanding and acceptance of the conditions contained herein.
    ​[bullet]By signing, the Plague Doctor does not become an employee in an organizational sense; SCP-049 remains a contained object with limited rights defined in this document.
    ​[bullet]The rights, privileges, and duties of the Plague Doctor are limited exclusively by the provisions of this contract and the directives of facility leadership (facility director, head of scientific services).
    
    ​[head=3]4. RIGHTS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
    ​[bullet]The Foundation shall provide basic conditions of containment: safety, nutrition, medical support, as well as the ability to conduct approved research sessions under staff supervision.
    ​[bullet]The Plague Doctor is permitted to make written and verbal statements to facility staff and scientists within bounds that do not conflict with instructions from staff of the corresponding clearance level (facility director, head of scientific services, head of Security).
    ​[bullet]Other privileges are granted only with permission from the head of scientific services or the facility director.
    
    ​[head=3]4.1. SPECIAL PERMISSIONS FOR SCP-049 REQUESTS[/head]
    ​[bold]Right to Make Requests[/bold]
    SCP-049 has the right to submit requests for limited items and "patients" (Class-D personnel) exclusively through clearance level 3 personnel and above.
    
    Authorized items for medical procedures:
    ​[bullet]basic surgical instruments (scalpel, retractor, gloves, etc.);
    ​[bullet]basic medicines (bruise kits, ointments, etc.) — strictly under the control of scientists or Security;
    ​[bullet]Additional items may be added to the list only with written permission from the facility director or the head of scientific services.
    
    ​[bold]Patients (Class-D)[/bold]
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 has the right to request the provision of test subjects (Class-D) for conducting "operations" or research.
    ​[bullet]The number of simultaneously provided D-Class persons is determined by the facility director and may not exceed the limit set by internal protocols.
    ​[bullet]All actions of SCP-049 involving D-Class are conducted exclusively under the observation of scientists or Security.
    
    ​[bold]Restrictions and Conditions[/bold]
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 has no right to independently choose specific D-Class persons or items. The decision is made by Foundation staff, except for the items authorized in section 4.1 of this contract.
    ​[bullet]Requests are processed in the normal chain and may be denied without explanation in the case of security threats, emergencies, shortages of resources, or at the discretion of leadership.
    ​[bullet]The provision of items and patients is not a right of SCP-049, but merely an option available when containment and security requirements are met.
    
    ​[bold]Abuse and Violations[/bold]
    ​[bullet]If SCP-049 engages in aggressive or manipulative behavior during a request, it loses the right to further applications for a period set by the facility director or head of scientific services.
    ​[bullet]If provided items or D-Class are used outside the scope of an experiment, immediate intervention by Security, item confiscation, and suppression measures shall be applied.
    
    ​[head=3]5. RESTRICTIONS AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
    ​[bullet]The Plague Doctor has no right to demand actions from staff that conflict with directives from the facility director, head of scientific services, or Security. Its words have no command authority.
    ​[bullet]The Plague Doctor must refrain from actions that pose a threat to staff life or facility integrity.
    ​[bullet]Manipulative, aggressive, or demonstratively demanding behavior by the Plague Doctor is considered a breach of contract terms and is grounds for disciplinary measures.
    ​[bullet]In an emergency, staff and facility safety takes precedence over the convenience of the Plague Doctor; its requests and privileges may be temporarily suspended without alternative.
    
    ​[head=3]6. DUTIES AND RIGHTS OF FOUNDATION STAFF[/head]
    ​[bullet]Staff must treat the Plague Doctor respectfully and professionally, but without granting any "special status".
    ​[bullet]Staff must abide by the terms of this contract and carry out protective instructions.
    ​[bullet]Security has the right to apply restraining measures (suppression devices, amnestics, isolation, use of force) in cases of contract violation or when there is a threat to life/safety.
    ​[bullet]Upon discovering attempts at escape or significant contract violations, the facility director and head of scientific services have priority in taking action.
    
    ​[head=3]7. PROCEDURES DURING EMERGENCIES[/head]
    ​[bullet]In the event of immediate threat to staff life or a major breach, priority actions are: threat localization, suppression (lethal or non-lethal by decision of the facility director or head of Security), object isolation, administration of amnestics, and restoration procedures.
    ​[bullet]If the Plague Doctor behaves aggressively and fewer than two SCP-049-2 are present, the threat is considered manageable; when two or more SCP-049-2 are present, additional protocols for restriction and use of fire are implemented.
    
    ​[head=3]8. INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATION[/head]
    ​[bold]Confidentiality[/bold]
    ​[bullet]All internal Foundation information (radio traffic, documents, protocols, personnel personal records, internal reports) is classified and intended exclusively for staff with the appropriate clearance level.
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 has no legal access to Foundation data, except for information directly conveyed in the context of experiments or communication with staff.
    
    ​[bold]Ban on Communications Equipment[/bold]
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 is prohibited from owning or using headsets, radios, intercoms, terminals, or any other communication devices that allow receiving or transmitting staff official information.
    ​[bullet]Any communication device found on SCP-049 or in its containment chamber is subject to immediate confiscation.
    
    ​[bold]Information Isolation[/bold]
    ​[bullet]Staff are required to ensure SCP-049 has no access to classified information.
    ​[bullet]If SCP-049 accidentally witnesses or learns information not intended for it, that information is deemed non-binding for SCP-049 and cannot be used as justification in requests or negotiations.
    
    ​[bold]Liability[/bold]
    ​[bullet]Attempts by SCP-049 to use Foundation classified information (including blackmail or threats) constitute a contract violation and result in immediate suppression measures and temporary isolation.
    ​[bullet]Breach of confidentiality by staff (for example, a headset left in the containment chamber) is recorded as an official error, and the responsible staff is subject to disciplinary action.
    
    ​[head=3]9. DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS AND SANCTIONS[/head]
    ​[bullet]For violation of contract terms, the Foundation may apply one or more of the following measures: verbal warning, isolation, forced sedation, transfer to heightened containment status, temporary or permanent limitation of privileges.
    ​[bullet]In cases of repeated or severe violations, lethal measures may be applied at the discretion of the facility director.
    
    ​[head=3]9.1. VIOLATION BY FOUNDATION STAFF[/head]
    In the event Foundation staff violate contract terms (using excessive force, depriving SCP-049 of rights and privileges explicitly set in the agreement, or ignoring agreed terms without an emergency), SCP-049 has the right to:
    
    ​[bullet]file an official complaint through the assigned curator (scientist, head of scientific services, or authorized level 3+ personnel).
    
    ​[bold]If the violation is confirmed:[/bold]
    ​[bullet]Responsible Foundation staff may face disciplinary action (demotion, clearance revocation, transfer to D-Class, internal investigation).
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 receives compensation in the form of restoration of violated privileges and an additional opportunity (for example, one unscheduled research session, greater freedom in requesting minor supplies).
    
    ​[bold]In the case of repeated contract violations by Foundation staff:[/bold]
    ​[bullet]SCP-049 may temporarily decline participation in tests/research until the conflict is resolved.
    ​[bullet]In so doing, SCP-049 must remain within the containment chamber and refrain from actions that threaten facility safety.
    ​[bullet]In an emergency (ESO), Foundation actions that interfere with SCP-049 privileges or comforts are not considered violations if they are directly aimed at saving staff lives or localizing a threat.
    
    ​[head=3]10. AMENDMENT AND TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT[/head]
    ​[bullet]Any changes to the contract are made only with written permission of the facility director and approval of the head of scientific services.
    ​[bullet]The contract may be terminated by decision of the facility director in the event of repeated serious violations by SCP-049 or upon change of object status.
    ​[bullet]Upon termination of the contract, all privileges of SCP-049 are revoked, and it is transferred to standard containment status.
